 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Keep practicing, it gets much easier. A good way to build it up is from line drawing, starting with simple lines for the eyes and then filling in. Pencil or pencil caliper, one end of which you can move back and forth, gives much more control than pencil. You can get very thin lines, which look lot older than they are. Use a sharp pencil and press firmly. Hold it with tip against your fingertip so it doesn't slip, and push straight down, not scribbled side to side. Enjoy the feeling of improvement and you' be drawing faces in no time.",
